WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.802 --> 00:00:05.959
The next day Jackie clipped on Howler's leash. "Grandma, I'm going to Hudson's house. He's

2
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:11.284
going to help me with Howler's training." "Good idea," Grandma said. "Hudson's one of the

3
00:00:11.285 --> 00:00:17.355
best young handlers I've seen." Jackie nodded. "He is a good handler. And he knows

4
00:00:17.356 --> 00:00:28.285
beagles really well." After yesterday, she hoped she'd get good at handling beagles soon too.

5
00:00:28.286 --> 00:00:41.506
As she approached Hudson's house, Jackie could see him at the obstacle course. Howler whined

6
00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:45.597
as they got closer, excited by another dog's scent. "No," Jackie commanded. "Stand and wait."

7
00:00:45.598 --> 00:00:54.249
Suddenly Bart's head popped from the end of a long tunnel. Howler immediately started barking.

8
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.657
Bart looked over, distracted by Howler's yipping. "No," Jackie repeated. "Howler, stand and wait." Hudson

9
00:00:57.658 --> 00:01:03.156
quickly got Bart's attention back, and they finished the course. Howler quivered with excitement as

10
00:01:03.157 --> 00:01:09.901
he watched the other dog race along, but he stayed at Jackie's side. "Sorry for

11
00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:16.749
the interruption," Jackie said when Hudson brought Bart over. "But you did offer to help

12
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:24.400
me with Howler!" Hudson grinned. "Glad to help. Do you mind if Bart and I

13
00:01:24.401 --> 00:01:30.962
run through the course once more? Move Howler right next to the ring. It will

14
00:01:30.963 --> 00:01:38.398
be good practice for Bart. He has to learn to stay focused." Jackie brought Howler

15
00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:45.796
to ringside as Hudson took Bart back to the starting line. Hudson made Bart sit

16
00:01:45.797 --> 00:01:53.121
and look at him as he talked. To Jackie, it seemed like a long discussion.

17
00:01:53.122 --> 00:02:03.353
She couldn't help giggling. Bart actually seemed to be following the conversation! "That's how you

18
00:02:03.354 --> 00:02:06.676
pay attention, Howler!" she said. Finally Hudson and Bart were ready. "Stand and wait," Jackie

19
00:02:06.677 --> 00:02:13.848
commanded. She wanted Howler to get used to standing near a show ring. Judges were

20
00:02:13.849 --> 00:02:21.078
always watching dogs and handlers, and a standing dog looked better than one that was

21
00:02:21.079 --> 00:02:23.686
sitting. "Go!" Hudson said. Bart took off like he was chasing a rabbit. He jumped

22
00:02:23.687 --> 00:02:35.921
over two bars and went under a third. Hudson raced beside the dog, calling out

23
00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:43.563
commands. Bart leaped onto a table and stopped. As soon as Hudson gave the command,

24
00:02:43.564 --> 00:02:54.559
Bart leaped down and barreled ahead. He went through a tunnel and over a long

25
00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.977
jump. "Yip!" Howler pranced excitedly. "No. Stand and wait," Jackie said. Howler obeyed, but Jackie

26
00:02:57.978 --> 00:03:08.988
could still feel his tense excitement as they watched Bart cross the finish line. "Nice!"

27
00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:11.625
Jackie called. "Thanks." Hudson gave Bart a treat. "Bart didn't even flinch when Howler barked."

28
00:03:11.626 --> 00:03:18.791
"His focus is amazing!" Jackie said. "So how's it going with Howler?" Hudson asked. "He's

29
00:03:18.792 --> 00:03:26.054
doing okay. He doesn't always pay attention—I have to really watch him." "That's what a

30
00:03:26.055 --> 00:03:32.529
good handler does—adjusts to the dog," Hudson said. "Let's see you stack him. Do you

31
00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:41.791
want to use the platform?" "Let's try the ground," Jackie said. "We have to learn

32
00:03:41.792 --> 00:03:51.778
both methods. Will you keep Bart in the ring while I practice with Howler? That'll

33
00:03:51.779 --> 00:04:00.272
test his focus." "Sure. Good idea." Jackie led Howler into the ring with Bart walking

34
00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:12.923
behind them. First, they circled the ring. Whenever Howler tried to look back, Jackie commanded,

35
00:04:12.924 --> 00:04:17.236
"Go," to bring his attention forward. "That was good," Hudson said after a few times

36
00:04:17.237 --> 00:04:22.827
around the ring. "Now bring him up," he called in an official tone, like a

37
00:04:22.828 --> 00:04:37.747
judge's. Jackie brought Howler to the center of the ring to stack him. She

38
00:04:37.748 --> 00:04:41.148
knelt and slipped one hand beneath Howler's jaw to control his head. Her other hand

39
00:04:41.149 --> 00:04:48.385
was on his tail. "Stay." "Speak," Hudson whispered to Bart. Bart obeyed. "Yip!" "Yip! Yip!"

40
00:04:48.386 --> 00:04:54.225
Howler wanted to see his new friend. Jackie held the dog's head firmly forward. "Stay."

41
00:04:54.226 --> 00:05:05.705
When Howler finally stayed still, Jackie rewarded him with a treat. "Stay," she commanded again,

42
00:05:05.706 --> 00:05:16.210
adjusting his back feet. Judge Hudson grinned, walking to Howler's side. He ran his hands

43
00:05:16.211 --> 00:05:22.192
down Howler's back and legs. He bent to look for wrinkles around the dog's neck.

44
00:05:22.193 --> 00:05:26.626
Beagles were supposed to have smooth necks. "Try holding his head a teeny bit higher,"

45
00:05:26.627 --> 00:05:31.115
Hudson said. Jackie gently lifted Howler's head a fraction of an inch. "That's better." Hudson

46
00:05:31.116 --> 00:05:40.174
stepped back. Howler looked at him, his face showing his excitement. "Yip!" "Stay," Jackie commanded.

47
00:05:40.175 --> 00:05:46.265
Howler didn't move and Jackie smiled. "That was great!" Hudson said. "Remember what I said

48
00:05:46.266 --> 00:05:52.509
about beagles showing a lot of personality? The judge won't deduct points for it, as

49
00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:59.412
long as the handler maintains control. And that's what you did." Jackie nodded, pleased. "Go

50
00:05:59.413 --> 00:06:07.072
around the ring again," Hudson said. "We'll judge his gait now." "Go!" Jackie commanded, starting

51
00:06:07.073 --> 00:06:13.324
off quickly. Jackie was halfway around the ring, when Hudson said, "Stop." Jackie halted, knowing

52
00:06:13.325 --> 00:06:21.483
what was coming. "He's pacing instead of trotting," Hudson said. Jackie frowned. "Am I going

53
00:06:21.484 --> 00:06:31.559
too slow or too fast? I can't figure it out." "I'm not sure. Why don't

54
00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:36.731
you try a courtesy circle first." "Okay." A courtesy circle was a tight circle, which

55
00:06:36.732 --> 00:06:43.635
handlers often did before starting around the ring. It helped them to get a dog

56
00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:48.696
moving properly before the judges started watching. "Go," Jackie said, turning Howler in a small

57
00:06:48.697 --> 00:06:56.362
circle before going around the ring. "Yes!" she thought. "We're trotting!" Then she felt a

58
00:06:56.363 --> 00:07:03.703
change in the dog's movement. He was pacing again! She stopped, letting out a heavy

59
00:07:03.704 --> 00:07:13.285
groan. "Let me try," Hudson said. Howler and Hudson circled the ring, the dog smoothly

60
00:07:13.286 --> 00:07:15.838
trotting the entire time. Jackie tried again. Halfway around, Howler started pacing. Jackie stopped, frustrated.

61
00:07:15.839 --> 00:07:23.496
"Grr," she complained. "What's the matter with this dog?" Hudson shrugged. "I'm not sure. But

62
00:07:23.497 --> 00:07:30.842
it's not a dog problem—it's a handler problem." Jackie felt stung. "I never had this

63
00:07:30.843 --> 00:07:38.239
problem with Poke—or any of Grandma's other dogs!" she snapped. "You've never handled this dog

64
00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:46.154
before," Hudson replied calmly. "You're still getting used to working together." Tears suddenly pricked at

65
00:07:46.155 --> 00:07:54.153
Jackie's eyes. She'd thought Hudson was going to help her, not criticize her. Plus, the

66
00:07:54.154 --> 00:08:01.820
show was just a few weeks away, and she had no clue how to fix

67
00:08:01.821 --> 00:08:09.155
this problem with Howler. "I made a big mistake," she blurted out. "I should have

68
00:08:09.156 --> 00:08:16.218
listened to Grandma instead of you. I don't like this breed." Hudson cocked his head

69
00:08:16.219 --> 00:08:23.630
and gave her a puzzled look. "That's ridiculous, Jackie. You can't blame an entire breed

70
00:08:23.631 --> 00:08:34.880
because you're having trouble handling one of them." Her temper flared. "Oh, so you think

71
00:08:34.881 --> 00:08:45.201
I'm not a good handler?" "I didn't say that," Hudson said. "You just need to—"

72
00:08:45.202 --> 00:08:54.886
Jackie didn't hear the rest. She was already running back to the farm with Howler.

